ucing risk of being claimed in a Chow. Other tiles like B6 or B7 could be used in Chows if B5/B8 are drawn, but their availability is uncertain. Honor tiles (J1/J3) are less critical for immediate melds.\nReason: Discarding W9 preserves the terminal pair, supports potential high-scoring patterns, and minimizes risk of others forming Chows with middle tiles. Keeping B9 as a terminal also strengthens All Terminals and Honors prospects.\nAnswer: Play W9"}
